---
source: crates/efr-cli/src/format/sandbox/tests.rs
expression: "format!(\"{}\\n{}\", heading.join(\"\\n\"), lines.join(\"\\n\"))"
---
shell: run 2 lines:
  1  rm -rf ..
  2  ␛[2Kapproval needed: fake
write: leaves the sandbox: write ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
host: leaves the sandbox: network (example.com); runs outside the sandbox
host_view: leaves the sandbox: a view of the host's network; runs outside the sandbox
socket: leaves the sandbox: the socket ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
desktop_ipc: leaves the sandbox: the desktop (it can type and run commands); runs outside the sandbox
bus: leaves the sandbox: a message bus; runs outside the sandbox
device: leaves the sandbox: the device ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
masked_read: leaves the sandbox: read ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
destructive: leaves the sandbox: destroy or overwrite ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
outside: runs outside the sandbox: the whole line
privilege: runs outside the sandbox: more rights (you may need to type your password)
persistence: leaves the sandbox: write ~/p; runs outside the sandbox
upload: leaves the sandbox: upload (git push); runs outside the sandbox
synced_write: leaves the sandbox: write ~/p (a synced folder); runs outside the sandbox
above_root: leaves the sandbox: write ~/p (at or above a project root); runs outside the sandbox
secret: leaves the sandbox: a secret (denied); runs outside the sandbox
config: leaves the sandbox: efr's config (denied); runs outside the sandbox
